      "writtenOn": "2026-07-01T05:57:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e How was this before this CL?\n\nI uploaded test only CL in\nhttps://gn-review.git.corp.google.com/c/gn/+/23581/5/src/gn/ninja_target_writer_unittest.cc#613\nso this part isn\u0027t changed by this change.\n\n\u003e Btw, I wanted to represent data deps using phony like this instead of order only deps for building the target without waiting for the data deps to be build. https://crbug.com/gn/413507213.\n\nDo we want to use validation deps rather than order only deps for data_deps? Also I\u0027m not sure how you use phony to make difference for order of build dependency.",
      "parentUuid": "1cf9a633_8b24666a",
      "revId": "5b91b30855bf1daed20399860202fd4524c0a4a2",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a10db0e9_b51aef9c",
        "filename": "src/gn/ninja_target_writer_unittest.cc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 613,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003017
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-01T06:37:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Do we want to use validation deps rather than order only deps for data_deps? \n\nNo, that proposal was rejected when we discussed it with gn-dev@ before.\n\n\u003e how you use phony to make difference for order of build dependency.\n\nThe problem I saw was building a target is waiting for data deps to be built, even though the data deps don\u0027t need to be ready when building the target. This is to ensure that data deps are built when the target is built. This is problematic when building the data deps takes long time. If you can build the target and the data deps in parallel, it would already be an improvement.",
      "parentUuid": "deb011d5_6ea72460",
      "revId": "5b91b30855bf1daed20399860202fd4524c0a4a2",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d8d584d8_9b8ca4de",
        "filename": "src/gn/ninja_target_writer_unittest.cc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 613,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-01T10:07:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think using phony doesn\u0027t simply solve that problem as phony is just alias of actual build targets.",
      "parentUuid": "a10db0e9_b51aef9c",
      "revId": "5b91b30855bf1daed20399860202fd4524c0a4a2",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b87856f_0d1233a6",
        "filename": "src/gn/ninja_target_writer_unittest.cc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 613,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003017
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-02T02:20:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My point is that the current implementation of data_deps forces targets to wait until its data deps to be build.\nA phony of target + data_deps can be used to build the data_deps in parallel with the target. I\u0027m not so sure how hard it is to refactor GN to do so, though.",
      "parentUuid": "d8d584d8_9b8ca4de",
      "revId": "5b91b30855bf1daed20399860202fd4524c0a4a2",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f717474_c50a9751",
        "filename": "src/gn/ninja_target_writer_unittest.cc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 613,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-06T07:58:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I guess what you want is if there is build config like below\n```\naction(\"A\") {\n  outputs \u003d [\"a.in\"]\n}\n\nexecutable(\"B\"){\n  sources \u003d [\"read_a.cc\"]\n  data_deps \u003d [\":A\"]\n}\n```\n\nYou may want to have phony target of B in ninja files like\n```\nbuild phony/B: phony B a.in\n```\n\nBut this doesn\u0027t work as we want if we pass `B` as build targets instead of `phony/B` to ninja. I don\u0027t know current status in GN, but we may still possible to move deps to A from compilation step of `read_a.cc` to link step.",
      "parentUuid": "2b87856f_0d1233a6",
      "revId": "5b91b30855bf1daed20399860202fd4524c0a4a2",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e80ca5f_9a53f9c9",
        "filename": "src/gn/ninja_target_writer_unittest.cc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 613,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003017
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-06T08:17:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, \"ninja B\" doesn\u0027t guarantee to build A. \n\n\u003e  we may still possible to move deps to A from compilation step of read_a.cc to link step.\n\nThat doesn\u0027t help the issue that I saw because the both target A and B were slow link steps.\n\nI guess we could still workaround by having A as a \"validation\" step of B, in addition to the `build phony/B: phony B a.in`, though.\n\ne.g.\n```\nbuild phony/B: phony B phony/A\nbuild B: ... |@ phony/A\n```",
      "parentUuid": "3f717474_c50a9751",
      "revId": "5b91b30855bf1daed20399860202fd4524c0a4a2",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
